  "notes": "The verb form of the noun {吹雪|ふぶき} (blizzard). Used impersonally to describe weather conditions, similar to how English uses \"it's snowing\" or \"it's blowing.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {激|はげ}しく{吹雪|ふぶ}く: to blow a fierce blizzard\n- {吹雪|ふぶ}き{始|はじ}める: to start blizzarding\n- {一日中|いちにちじゅう}{吹雪|ふぶ}いていた: it was a blizzard all day\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {吹雪|ふぶき}: blizzard (noun)\n- {雪|ゆき}が{降|ふ}る: to snow (without strong wind)\n- {猛吹雪|もうふぶき}: severe blizzard",
